{"subjectId":"dsa-basics","id":"stack","title":"Stack","group":"","order":14,"html":"<p>10 | 20 | 30 | 40 | --&gt; push(x) | pop()</p>\n<p>Last IN First OUT</p>\n<h4>Operations</h4>\n<p>isEmpty() : if stack is empty returns True</p>\n<p>push(x) : Insert an item to the top of Stack</p>\n<p>pop() : Removes an item from the top</p>\n<p>peek() : Returns top item</p>\n<p>size() : Returns the size</p>\n<p>UnderFlow : When pop() and peek() called no empty stack</p>\n<p>OverFlow : when push() called on a Full Stack</p>\n<p>Stack in Python</p>\n<p>1. Using List</p>\n<p>2. Using collection.deque</p>\n<p>3. Using queue.LIFOQueue (Advanced Topic)</p>\n<p>4. Using our own Implementation</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 1 : Using List\n\nstack = []\n\nstack.append('a')\nstack.append('b')\nstack.append('c')\n\nprint('Initial Stack')\nprint(stack)\n\nprint('\\nElements poped from stack')\nprint(stack.pop())\nprint(stack.pop())\nprint(stack.pop())\n\nprint('\\nStack after elements are poped')\nprint(stack)</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Method 2 : using deque\n\nfrom collections import deque\n\nstack = deque()\nstack.append('a')\nstack.append('b')\nstack.append('c')\n\nprint(stack.pop())\nprint(stack.pop())\n\ntop = stack[-1]\nprint(top)\n\nprint(len(stack))</code></pre></figure>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code># Linked List Implementation\n\nclass Node:\n  def __init__(self, value):\n    self.value = value\n    self.next = None\n\nclass myStack:\n  def __init__(self):\n    self.head = None\n    self.size = 0\n\n  def push(self, value):\n    node = Node(value)\n    if self.head:\n      node.next = self.head\n    self.head = node\n    self.size += 1\n\n  def pop(self):\n    if self.head:\n      temp = self.head\n      self.head = self.head.next\n      self.size -= 1\n      return temp.value\n    else:\n      return None\n\n  def peek(self):\n    if self.head:\n      return self.head.value\n    else:\n      return None\n\n  def sizes(self):\n    return self.size\n\ndef printList(head):\n  temp = head\n  while temp:\n    print(temp.value, end = \" \")\n    temp = temp.next\n\ns = myStack()\ns.push(1)\ns.push(2)\ns.push(3)\nprintList(s.head)\nprint()\nprint(s.sizes())\nprint(s.pop())\nprint(s.peek())</code></pre></figure>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3>Applications of Stack</h3>\n<p>1. Function calls</p>\n<p>2. Balanced parenthesis</p>\n<p>3. Reversing Items</p>\n<p>4. Infix to Postfix/prefix</p>\n<p>5. Evaluation of Postfix/prefix</p>\n<p>6. Stock spam problem</p>\n<p>7. Undo/Redo or Forward/Backward</p>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3>Check for Balanced parenthesis</h3>\n<div class=\"callout callout--example\">\n<div class=\"callout-label\"><i class=\"ti ti-terminal-2\"></i> Case Example</div>\n<p><strong>Input:</strong> s = '([])'<br><strong>Output:</strong> Yes<br><strong>Input:</strong> s = '([)]'<br><strong>Output:</strong> No</p>\n</div>\n<figure data-lang=\"py\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Python</figcaption><pre><code>def isBalanced(s):\n  stack = []\n  for x in expr:\n    if x in ['(', '{', '[']:\n      stack.append(x)\n    else:\n      if not stack:\n        return False\n      elif isMarching(stack[-1], x) == False:\n        return False\n      else:\n        stack.pop()\n  if not stack:\n    return True\n  else:\n    return False\n\ndef isMarching(a, b):\n  if a == '(' and b == ')':\n    return True\n  elif a == '{' and b == '}':\n    return True\n  elif a == '[' and b == ']':\n    return True\n  else:\n    return False\n\nexpr = input()\nif isBalanced(expr):\n  print('Yes')\nelse:\n  print('No')</code></pre></figure></section>"}